<!--
    Return Category radio group, injected into the Request Header form as a
    custom field. It is registered in manifest.json under
    controlConfiguration > "@com.sap.vocabularies.UI.v1.FieldGroup#RequestHeader"
    > fields, which is where Fiori elements looks up custom form fields (keyed
    by the facet's annotation target, not by the facet ID).

    Budget Zerorise and Budget Return to Central Fund are mutually exclusive,
    so they are backed by the single returnCategory_code property rather than
    two flags.

    Use %{...} rather than ${...} inside expression bindings here. Fiori
    elements runs this fragment through the XML preprocessor, which consumes
    ${...} before it reaches the control - on typed properties such as visible
    and selectedIndex that surfaces as a FormatException and the property
    silently falls back to its default. %{...} survives templating and is
    evaluated at runtime, which is also what the framework's own
    BindingToolkit emits.

    selectedIndex is one-way, so the write back happens in
    onReturnCategorySelect on the ObjectPage controller extension.

    Once Pending Approval (status_code 2), only Reason and Asset
    Status stay editable - this locks with the rest of the header/item
    fields (see annotations.cds), on top of the standard ui>/isEditable
    edit-mode check.

    A Project-budget Return is always Budget Zerorise - "Return to
    Central Fund" only makes sense for Non Project - so for
    budgetType_code 'P' the radio choice is replaced by a plain,
    non-interactive "Budget Zerorise" label instead of the group. The
    actual returnCategory_code value is force-set to 'Z' server-side
    regardless (see requests-before-create-logic.js), this is purely
    the display side of that same rule.

    A custom form field template is expected to render as a SINGLE
    control - the RadioButtonGroup and the Project-only Text label
    below are therefore wrapped in one VBox rather than left as two
    top-level siblings, which Fiori elements did not render at all
    (neither control showed, for either Budget Type).
-->
<core:FragmentDefinition
    xmlns="sap.m"
    xmlns:core="sap.ui.core"
    xmlns:form="sap.ui.layout.form">
    <VBox>
        <RadioButtonGroup
            id="returnCategoryGroup"
            columns="1"
            width="100%"
            visible="{= %{requestType_code} === 'R' &amp;&amp; %{budgetType_code} !== 'P' }"
            editable="{= %{ui>/isEditable} === true &amp;&amp; %{status_code} !== 2 }"
            selectedIndex="{= %{returnCategory_code} === 'Z' ? 0 : (%{returnCategory_code} === 'C' ? 1 : -1) }"
            select=".extension.virement.zuippsvirement.ext.controller.ObjectPageExt.onReturnCategorySelect">
            <!--
                The Central Fund option's label is longer than this form's
                default single-column width (it now carries the GL account
                suffix), so both buttons wrap instead of being clipped, and
                the group spans the full row width (see layoutData on the
                VBox below) rather than just one column, to give that text
                room.
            -->
            <RadioButton
                id="returnCategoryZerorise"
                text="{i18n>BudgetZerorise}"
                wrapping="true" />
            <RadioButton
                id="returnCategoryCentralFund"
                text="{i18n>BudgetReturnToCentralFund}"
                wrapping="true" />
        </RadioButtonGroup>
        <Text
            id="returnCategoryZeroriseOnly"
            text="{i18n>BudgetZerorise}"
            visible="{= %{requestType_code} === 'R' &amp;&amp; %{budgetType_code} === 'P' }" />
        <layoutData>
            <form:ColumnElementData cellsLarge="4" cellsSmall="4" />
        </layoutData>
    </VBox>
</core:FragmentDefinition>
